- Hey, what about her?

00:36:26.270 --> 00:36:27.560
- We'll take her to the neighbors, come on.

00:36:40.780 --> 00:36:41.480
- Why, Breen?

00:36:41.480 --> 00:36:42.300
- Why he...

00:36:42.300 --> 00:36:54.910
- Come on, Raleigh.

00:36:54.910 --> 00:36:56.290
- I say, sir, you've no right.

00:36:56.290 --> 00:36:58.520
- Shut up you, I'll make my own right.

00:36:58.520 --> 00:37:00.000
- Breen, you murdered one.

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:01.970
We've got the goods on you.

00:37:01.970 --> 00:37:06.970
Mr. Breen says you'll talk to him civilly or you'll leave his house.

00:37:06.970 --> 00:37:08.970
I'll talk to him civilly with a poke and a snoot.

00:37:08.970 --> 00:37:12.460
Breen, a man named Werner was murdered tonight.

00:37:12.460 --> 00:37:14.440
His mother will testify that you did it.

00:37:14.440 --> 00:37:23.400
Mr. Breen says why don't you arrest him again

00:37:23.400 --> 00:37:26.700
and make yourself the laughingstocks you were in the Garfield case.

00:37:26.700 --> 00:37:27.800
Why, you?

00:37:31.920 --> 00:37:38.400
If you're innocent, how do you explain the people who will identify you as the man on the scene of the crime?

00:37:38.400 --> 00:37:48.730
Mr. Breen says if you look at the matter calmly, it is easily explained.

00:37:48.730 --> 00:37:54.140
The watchman on the Garfield case was obviously drunk and might have identified anyone.

00:37:54.140 --> 00:38:00.000
And Mrs. Werner, after her son was murdered, probably had an hallucination caused by what she did.

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:01.000
been reading in the papers.

00:38:13.050 --> 00:38:15.990
Mr. Breen is very sorry to hear of young Werner's death.

00:38:16.410 --> 00:38:21.170
He liked the boy immensely, and he will do all he can in order to help to bring the murderer

00:38:21.170 --> 00:38:21.850
to justice.

00:38:22.650 --> 00:38:22.990
Thanks.

00:38:24.810 --> 00:38:26.270
Breen, where were you tonight at 8.30?

00:38:26.530 --> 00:38:30.000
Mr. Breen has had a very bad cold.

00:38:30.480 --> 00:38:34.160
He lay down at six o'clock and slept until the gentleman wakened him.

00:38:35.480 --> 00:38:35.760
Uh-huh.

00:39:27.200 --> 00:39:30.000
Say, why should Breen have a piano?

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:31.000
if he can't hear music.

00:39:32.130 --> 00:39:33.650
Mr. Breen has the piano

00:39:33.650 --> 00:39:35.170
for the enjoyment of his guests.

00:39:36.280 --> 00:39:36.700
Oh, yeah.

00:39:46.400 --> 00:39:53.230
Come on, Jack.

00:39:53.270 --> 00:39:54.290
There's nothing else for us to do here.

00:39:57.410 --> 00:39:58.090
Good night, Mr. Breen.

00:39:58.170 --> 00:39:59.430
I'm sorry we disturbed you.

00:40:09.470 --> 00:40:13.450
- Good night, gentlemen.

00:40:13.450 --> 00:40:27.930
- Say, what do you make of it, Jim?

00:40:27.930 --> 00:40:29.440
- I'd like to know how we could hear that piano

00:40:29.440 --> 00:40:30.000
when I couldn't get a phone.

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:31.660
tumbled out of him firing off a gun.

00:40:31.660 --> 00:40:33.440
- What makes you think he could hear me at the piano?

00:40:33.440 --> 00:40:34.660
- I was watching him.

00:40:34.660 --> 00:40:36.780
He heard you all right.

00:40:36.780 --> 00:40:37.770
- Where does that get us?

00:40:37.770 --> 00:40:39.440
- Gives me an idea.

00:40:39.440 --> 00:40:41.060
I'm gonna sleep on it, and if I feel the same way

00:40:41.060 --> 00:40:42.380
in the morning, I'm burning the squad over here

00:40:42.380 --> 00:40:43.220
for a showdown.

00:40:43.220 --> 00:40:44.140
- Yeah, but Chief.

00:40:44.140 --> 00:40:46.100
- See me at my office at nine o'clock in the morning.

00:40:46.100 --> 00:40:47.700
- Listen, can't you give me a tip of some kind?

00:40:47.700 --> 00:40:49.500
- Go on to discuss it, that's all it's up to say.

00:40:49.500 --> 00:40:51.190
- Well, listen, you know, I've been--

00:41:03.100 --> 00:41:04.560
That copper is onto something.

00:41:10.480 --> 00:41:21.960
You found out that that reporter guy is sweet on the crane thing.

00:41:22.590 --> 00:41:26.530
If you don't look out, you're going to spoil a swell racket just on account of a skirt.

00:42:02.300 --> 00:42:03.430
Hi, boys. Hi, Casey.

00:42:03.750 --> 00:42:05.950
Hey, wait a minute. Who do you want to see?

00:42:06.150 --> 00:42:07.630
Oh, Riley. I got a date with him this morning.

00:42:07.880 --> 00:42:08.640
Well, you won't see him.

00:42:08.760 --> 00:42:09.580
Yeah, who says so?

00:42:09.660 --> 00:42:11.300
I say so. He's dead.

00:42:12.890 --> 00:42:13.190
Riley?

00:42:14.570 --> 00:42:17.220
Yeah. The chief was found murdered early this morning.

00:42:17.970 --> 00:42:18.990
But where? How?

00:42:19.380 --> 00:42:22.190
You'd have to ask Hogan. He'd been put in charge of the precinct.

00:42:23.430 --> 00:42:25.940
I should have known it. Riley was on the brain.

00:42:26.250 --> 00:42:27.110
He had to get him.

00:42:36.680 --> 00:42:40.080
Hold on. How did it happen? Tell me about it.

00:42:40.790 --> 00:42:43.270
Riley's wife found him in bed at 7 o'clock.

00:42:44.330 --> 00:42:45.510
Strangled, like the other guys.

00:42:46.350 --> 00:42:48.460
How could the murderer get to him?

00:42:50.700 --> 00:42:51.060
Easy.

00:42:52.850 --> 00:42:55.410
Alleyway and a fire escape leading to his bedroom window.

00:42:56.350 --> 00:42:57.500
Now I know it's Green.

00:42:58.600 --> 00:42:58.940
Yeah?

00:43:00.320 --> 00:43:01.480
What are you going to do about it?

00:43:01.480 --> 00:43:07.130
You can't get anything on him.

00:43:07.130 --> 00:43:11.080
What a swell break I get.

00:43:11.080 --> 00:43:15.140
For 15 years, I've laid for this inspectorship,

00:43:15.140 --> 00:43:18.850
and now they hand it to me with five unsolved murders

00:43:18.850 --> 00:43:22.030
staring me in the face.

00:43:22.030 --> 00:43:24.420
What's the police commission got to say?

00:43:24.420 --> 00:43:26.860
They give me two weeks to find the murderer of Riley,

00:43:26.860 --> 00:43:28.960
or I'm canned.

00:43:28.960 --> 00:43:30.000
You can send me...

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:31.200
in your resignation right now.

00:43:32.090 --> 00:43:32.990
If you get anything on Green,

00:43:33.370 --> 00:43:34.290
he'll take care of you

00:43:34.290 --> 00:43:35.850
just as quick as he took care of Riley.

00:43:37.980 --> 00:43:38.380
Yeah.

00:43:40.400 --> 00:43:44.100
I wonder why he went after Riley.

00:43:44.900 --> 00:43:46.140
Riley found out some kind of clue

00:43:46.140 --> 00:43:47.320
at Green's house last night.

00:43:47.930 --> 00:43:48.890
He's gonna tell me about it this morning.

00:43:49.860 --> 00:43:50.660
Green got wise to him

00:43:50.660 --> 00:43:51.570
and bumped him off.

00:43:52.410 --> 00:43:53.460
What were you and Riley doing

00:43:53.460 --> 00:43:54.660
at Green's house last night?

00:43:54.950 --> 00:43:55.700
We went up there

00:43:55.700 --> 00:43:56.360
on the Werner murder.

00:43:56.720 --> 00:43:57.560
Couldn't get to first base.

00:43:57.740 --> 00:43:58.630
And what's the lowdown

00:43:58.630 --> 00:43:59.510
on that Werner case?

00:43:59.550 --> 00:44:00.000
I was so...

00:44:00.990 --> 00:44:02.190
He got Wernher for the same reason.

00:44:02.370 --> 00:44:03.330
Wernher got wise to his secret.

00:44:04.680 --> 00:44:05.980
I tell you, that guy Breen's a maniac.

00:44:06.760 --> 00:44:08.600
He'll kill anybody who finds out about him.

00:44:11.230 --> 00:44:15.760
I wonder who else might stumble onto that guy's secret.

00:44:17.390 --> 00:44:21.320
He might just as well tip him off to stay away.

00:44:25.220 --> 00:44:28.260
Jerry Crane.

00:44:28.590 --> 00:44:29.410
What about her?

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:31.220
She's been seeing Breen all the time.

00:44:31.460 --> 00:44:32.440
She might stumble onto a secret.

00:44:33.290 --> 00:44:34.980
I thought she was your girl.

00:44:35.340 --> 00:44:37.040
She used to be until this guy started to work on her.

00:44:37.770 --> 00:44:38.350
Hypnotizing her.

00:44:40.080 --> 00:44:40.920
I gotta do something.

00:44:42.340 --> 00:44:43.060
Say, wait a minute.

00:44:43.100 --> 00:44:44.020
Let me talk to her.

00:44:44.830 --> 00:44:46.830
I got away with these names.

00:44:47.330 --> 00:44:47.830
Yeah, all right.

00:44:48.820 --> 00:44:50.640
Say, give me the chronicle right quick.

00:44:50.880 --> 00:44:55.680
Yes, we know, but don't you realize the danger you're in?

00:44:56.330 --> 00:44:58.710
I'm sorry, Mr. Hogan, but I can't see it that way.

00:44:59.200 --> 00:45:00.000
I know Mr. Breen.

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:03.920
He couldn't possibly be gilly of the things you're talking about.

00:45:03.920 --> 00:45:07.500
But, Jerry, dear, don't you understand?

00:45:07.500 --> 00:45:08.330
We've been working on this thing.

00:45:08.330 --> 00:45:10.330
We can see things you can't.

00:45:10.330 --> 00:45:12.160
Jack, you should know better.

00:45:12.160 --> 00:45:15.050
When people go snooping around with wild ideas in their minds,

00:45:15.050 --> 00:45:17.050
the first thing you know, they begin to believe them.

00:45:17.050 --> 00:45:20.480
As a matter of fact, you're asking me to believe the rottenest things

00:45:20.480 --> 00:45:22.480
about one of the finest men I've ever met.

00:45:22.480 --> 00:45:24.480
We're not asking you to believe a thing.

00:45:24.480 --> 00:45:27.300
All we want you to do is to stop associating with Green.

00:45:27.300 --> 00:45:30.000
What do you mean, associating with Green?

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:33.300
Everybody's been talking about it. It's even made in the newspapers.

00:45:33.340 --> 00:45:35.450
All these visits he's been making to his house.

00:45:35.490 --> 00:45:38.690
Which only means that the gossipers and columnists and the other papers

00:45:38.730 --> 00:45:42.550
are following in the footsteps of Mr. Burton of the Chronicle.

00:45:42.590 --> 00:45:48.000
You're very foolish, risking your life for a woman's whim.

00:45:48.040 --> 00:45:52.310
Why, this is no whim and Jack knows it very well.

00:45:52.350 --> 00:45:54.310
I'm writing a series of articles on Mr. Breen.

00:45:54.350 --> 00:45:56.780
I'm being well paid and I need the money badly.

00:45:56.820 --> 00:45:59.730
All right then, chuck your articles.

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:04.780
give you what you need. We've been through all that, Jack. How many more articles have you got to

00:46:04.780 --> 00:46:10.510
write? You've written a dozen now for a guy who doesn't even write a short obituary. Well, that's

00:46:10.510 --> 00:46:17.760
really my business. Supposing I make it my business? Now, see here, Mr. Burton. I like Mr.

00:46:17.820 --> 00:46:24.860
Breen, and I'm going to see him whenever I want to. But, Jerry, listen, honey, don't go now.

00:46:25.390 --> 00:46:29.110
Have dinner with me and talk it over. As a matter of fact, I'm having dinner with Mr. Breen.

00:46:30.280 --> 00:46:34.000
Don't you realize that bird has bumped off two men in the last twenty-four hours?

00:46:34.000 --> 00:46:35.670
Don't that mean anything to you?

00:46:35.670 --> 00:46:37.680
- What? - Yes.

00:46:37.680 --> 00:46:46.570
No more than it would to Jack or any other reporter covering an assignment.

00:46:46.570 --> 00:46:49.550
- Even if it were true. - But, Jerry...

00:46:49.550 --> 00:46:51.700
Oh, I'll tell you what I'll do.

00:46:51.700 --> 00:46:55.010
If it'll make you feel any better, I'll ask Mr. Breen not to murder me.

00:46:55.010 --> 00:46:57.620
Uh, Jerry, listen. Supposing you should stumble onto a secret?

00:46:57.620 --> 00:47:00.000
I won't, my dear. I'll pick my steps.

00:47:05.240 --> 00:47:06.660
Hogan, I don't care what she says.

00:47:06.880 --> 00:47:09.020
She's liable to go up to the house tonight and never be heard of again.

00:47:10.520 --> 00:47:11.640
Ted Casey in here.

00:47:12.270 --> 00:47:13.310
We've got to do something.

00:47:13.780 --> 00:47:16.000
Calm down now and let me handle this, will you?

00:47:16.390 --> 00:47:17.130
You want me, Keith?

00:47:17.350 --> 00:47:19.630
Yeah, I want you and Sullivan to watch that Breen house.

00:47:20.540 --> 00:47:21.900
Jerry Crane's going over there tonight.

00:47:21.960 --> 00:47:24.360
If anything suspicious happens, telephone me here.

00:47:24.540 --> 00:47:25.570
Oh, thanks, Hogan.

00:47:25.770 --> 00:47:26.430
You're a pal.

00:47:26.670 --> 00:47:28.250
I'll go along with the boys and help them cover the house.

00:47:28.720 --> 00:47:30.000
Yeah, and I'm going to get into a jam.

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:34.480
I guess the Commission's ordered to have anybody watching us is suspected of a felony.

00:47:34.480 --> 00:47:39.670
Felony? Say, what do you think this is, a picnic?

00:47:39.670 --> 00:47:44.530
I don't like dames. I never did like dames.

00:47:44.530 --> 00:47:51.010
I'm gonna get canned for protectin' one when I oughta be givin' her a good swift kick in the... slacks.

00:47:51.010 --> 00:47:52.500
You're right, Chief.

00:48:17.080 --> 00:48:18.460
Queen dame just went in the house?

00:48:18.600 --> 00:48:20.940
Yeah. I was talking to Burton when she went by.

00:48:21.380 --> 00:48:23.470
Just our luck. She's a good-looking dame.

00:48:23.870 --> 00:48:25.430
We'll ever have to wait here for hours.

00:48:25.530 --> 00:48:26.530
Well, it's Hogan's orders.

00:48:27.460 --> 00:48:28.680
You better keep circling the block.

00:48:39.470 --> 00:48:41.940
- But I'm finishing the articles, Mr. Breen.

00:48:41.940 --> 00:48:44.340
I really don't think I should impose on you anymore.

00:49:14.240 --> 00:49:16.840
I can't see any reason why I should stop coming up here.

00:49:17.600 --> 00:49:19.880
You seem like an old friend whom I've known for years.

00:49:54.920 --> 00:49:56.660
- A cigarette, Casey? - Sure.

00:50:05.850 --> 00:50:07.780
I got a hunch that guy spotted us.

00:50:07.780 --> 00:50:10.010
Well, so long.

00:50:10.010 --> 00:50:11.040
So long.

00:50:53.710 --> 00:50:57.720
I told you about that dame, there are a couple of dicks outside watching the house.

00:52:02.810 --> 00:52:11.010
Phone Hogan. Come on, Casey.

00:52:34.990 --> 00:52:47.000
- Gentlemen, get in there.

00:52:47.000 --> 00:52:48.270
- Jerry Crane.

00:52:48.270 --> 00:52:49.530
- Now listen there, you can-- - You shut up.

00:52:49.530 --> 00:52:53.880
- What have you done with it?

00:52:53.880 --> 00:52:56.330
- Casey, I'm gonna search the house.

00:52:56.330 --> 00:52:57.650
Keep these two birds covered. - Right.

00:53:15.640 --> 00:53:21.620
I'll have the squad on your toes.

00:53:22.000 --> 00:53:23.270
We're leaving.

00:53:23.510 --> 00:53:24.450
We're on our way.

00:53:44.490 --> 00:53:48.000
Hey, do you think I'm gonna believe any of that junk you've been writing?

00:53:48.000 --> 00:53:53.360
Well, here, I'm gonna get the truth out of you if I have to choke it out of you.

00:53:53.360 --> 00:54:00.000
- Any luck? - Not a sign of her anyplace.

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:02.420
Oh, it's empty. What's he say?

00:54:02.420 --> 00:54:05.060
Oh, that guy can lie faster than he can write.

00:54:05.060 --> 00:54:06.760
He says Miss Crum here at all today.

00:54:06.760 --> 00:54:08.260
Didn't you tell him we saw her come in?

00:54:08.260 --> 00:54:11.950
Yes, he says that's a maid, and she went out the back door.

00:54:11.950 --> 00:54:15.610
Say, if you know what's good for you, you'll come across.

00:54:15.610 --> 00:54:18.500
The minute I find out anything's happened to that girl,

00:54:18.500 --> 00:54:20.130
you'll be on the business end of a bullet.

00:55:24.220 --> 00:55:27.850
- Hey, Ken, that racket.

00:55:27.850 --> 00:55:29.600
- You just ain't got no ear for music.

00:55:30.830 --> 00:55:33.600
Besides, I think a lot better when I play.

00:55:33.600 --> 00:55:35.510
Yeah?

00:55:35.510 --> 00:55:41.680
Say, I got a hunch I've got the secret of this mystery right at my fingertips.

00:55:41.680 --> 00:55:43.890
I tell you, Jerry's right here in this house.

00:55:43.890 --> 00:55:47.760
Yeah, that's right.

00:55:47.760 --> 00:55:54.230
Say, didn't Riley say something about getting a clue around here?

00:55:54.230 --> 00:55:57.730
Yeah, he said something about Breen being able to hear the piano.

00:55:57.730 --> 00:55:58.870
Yeah.

00:56:08.220 --> 00:56:10.260
Well, I don't know what kind of a clue he'd get out of that.

00:56:12.430 --> 00:56:17.060
Eh, whoopee.

00:56:32.940 --> 00:56:33.780
Get that guy!

00:56:40.960 --> 00:56:46.120
Take it easy.

00:56:47.480 --> 00:56:48.030
You all right?

00:56:48.390 --> 00:56:49.620
I'm just a bit shaky.

00:56:54.880 --> 00:56:57.100
Take it easy here, boy.

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:02.670
Oh, I told you not to trust this fellow, didn't I?

00:57:03.940 --> 00:57:05.120
Thought you said she wasn't here.

00:57:06.920 --> 00:57:08.390
The other guy's dead, Chief.

00:57:08.920 --> 00:57:09.200
Yeah?

00:57:09.900 --> 00:57:11.410
Watch him.

00:57:19.000 --> 00:57:19.300
Well.

00:57:33.040 --> 00:57:35.040
They're just like as two peas in a pod.

00:57:38.090 --> 00:57:39.650
They can't both be deaf and dumb.

00:57:42.340 --> 00:57:44.740
I wonder which one of them we plugged.

00:57:49.180 --> 00:57:52.030
Hey, can you talk or can't you?

00:57:52.410 --> 00:57:54.730
Now, I'm going to tell you right now, I won't believe a word you say.

00:57:57.490 --> 00:57:58.910
All right, gentlemen.

00:58:00.220 --> 00:58:01.180
I'm ready to talk.

00:58:04.910 --> 00:58:09.060
It's my duty to tell you that anything you might say will be used against you.

00:58:10.080 --> 00:58:11.660
Nothing will ever be used against me.

00:58:12.260 --> 00:58:12.640
No?

00:58:13.690 --> 00:58:15.550
Well, begin and don't talk so much.

00:58:18.360 --> 00:58:19.080
Well, we're waiting.

00:58:22.030 --> 00:58:27.060
The mystery of the Sphinx, as you gentlemen of the press dummied the honor of calling me,

00:58:28.010 --> 00:58:29.430
should now be really quite obvious.

00:58:30.920 --> 00:58:38.030
Whenever I found it necessary to remove an obstacle, it was quite simple to establish a perfect alibi.

00:58:38.030 --> 00:58:44.290
My twin brother temporarily assumed my identity, and he being a real deaf newt,

00:58:44.290 --> 00:58:50.780
well, of course, would naturally discredit any witnesses who might testify that he had spoken to them.

00:58:50.780 --> 00:58:59.700
How successfully my little scheme worked could be attested to by the police departments of other cities beside your own.

00:59:00.990 --> 00:59:09.320
My only oversight was my inability to foresee an inspector with a talent for the piano.

00:59:09.320 --> 00:59:15.430
So you admit that you got Garfield, eh?

00:59:15.430 --> 00:59:17.420
Unfortunately, I did.

00:59:17.420 --> 00:59:21.680
I formed a stock pool with four other brokers with Garfield.

00:59:21.680 --> 00:59:26.830
They didn't like the way I did business and threatened to go to the district attorney.

00:59:26.830 --> 00:59:29.200
Well, I had to protect myself.

00:59:29.200 --> 00:59:30.000
Why?

00:59:30.030 --> 00:59:36.240
Of course. And Werner and Riley, what about them?

00:59:36.240 --> 00:59:39.730
Werner was a skunk. He tried to double-cross me.

00:59:39.730 --> 00:59:42.770
Riley got suspicious about the piano.

00:59:42.770 --> 00:59:47.670
And, uh, Jenks. Was he in on this? Where is that guy?

00:59:47.670 --> 00:59:53.560
Jenks is miles away by now. Suppose you ask him.

00:59:53.560 --> 00:59:55.290
You won't talk, eh?

00:59:55.290 --> 01:00:00.000
Well, suppose we get going before you get a chance to get miles away.

01:00:01.280 --> 01:00:02.000
Snap him on him.

01:00:08.770 --> 01:00:13.690
I'm ready.

01:00:32.590 --> 01:00:33.190
He's dead.

01:00:34.640 --> 01:00:36.830
He's been hurt there yet.

01:00:49.440 --> 01:00:58.210
There you are.

01:01:00.320 --> 01:01:00.600
Careful.

01:01:02.470 --> 01:01:03.370
What's that, a souvenir?

01:01:03.910 --> 01:01:05.790
It's how he died. Poison.

01:01:06.350 --> 01:01:08.050
What are you trying to do, kid me?

01:01:08.410 --> 01:01:09.690
It's a medieval poison ring.

01:01:10.150 --> 01:01:12.500
If you press it right, the plunger comes out and pricks the finger.

01:01:13.650 --> 01:01:14.050
Oh.

01:01:16.440 --> 01:01:18.920
You know, I suspected something like that all the time.

01:01:19.710 --> 01:01:20.070
Yeah.

01:01:22.720 --> 01:01:24.060
Sullivan, take care of that, will you?

01:01:25.290 --> 01:01:27.790
And Jack, I guess I've been pretty stupid.

01:01:28.240 --> 01:01:30.000
Well, I'll let it go this time, but from now on...

01:01:30.060 --> 01:01:32.630
- Come on, I'm wearing the brains in this family.

01:01:32.630 --> 01:01:34.370
- This family?

01:01:34.370 --> 01:01:35.930
Aren't you working a little fast?

01:01:35.930 --> 01:01:37.510
- You bet I am.

01:01:37.510 --> 01:01:38.990
We're getting married.

01:01:38.990 --> 01:01:40.470
I'm gonna raise chickens.

01:01:40.470 --> 01:01:46.350
You're gonna raise, how 'bout it, Mama?

01:01:46.350 --> 01:01:47.890
- All right, well, I'll see you pretty quick.

01:01:47.890 --> 01:01:49.150
You take care of me.

01:01:49.150 --> 01:01:49.990
- All right, excuse me.

01:01:49.990 --> 01:01:51.630
- All right, I'll go on.

01:01:51.630 --> 01:01:57.110
Well, Inspector, I guess you keep your job after all, huh?

01:01:57.110 --> 01:01:59.170
- Yeah, yeah.

01:01:59.170 --> 01:02:00.000
Can I keep the job?

01:02:03.640 --> 01:02:07.960
And you all laugh when I sit down at the piano.

01:02:11.840 --> 01:02:13.320
He-he-he.
